                        ||   SETUP   ||

                          ** PART 1 **

  Plinko is written in AREXX and compiled with "REXX compiler Plus".
  You need to have both Arexx and the Rexx Plus environment running
  on your system to use this game. If you already have compiled Arexx
  games running on your system, or know that the REXX Plus environment
  is already active on your system, then skip to PART 2 NOW!!

  Still here? OK, to setup REXX PLUS, do the following :

  * If you don't have the program "RPStart" in your C: dir, then copy it
    there.

  * IF you don't have the program "RPHi" in your C: dir then copy it
    there.

  * copy the file "rexxplslib.library" to your LIBS: dir

  * If you don't have the program RPStart setup to run in your startup,
    then add the following line to your User-Startup OR Startup-sequence:

              C:RPStart

   Add it BEFORE the Loadwb command in the Startup-sequence or the bottom
   of the user-startup file.


                          ** PART 2 **

   BBBBS Setup :

    Rename the file "Plinko" to "Plinko.rexx" and copy it to your
    Rexxdoors directory.

   Trinity Setup :

    Copy the file "Plinko" to your OLP: directory.
    Add Plinko to your OLP menu (see Trinity doc, Online Programs)
    as any other Arexx game.

   DLG Setup :

    Copy the file "Plinko" to your Doors: directory.
    See the IFF picture (provided by Kurt Christ) that illustrates
    his setup for plinko named "Plinko.iff".

                  +++++ Setup Complete +++++

